comments:
@serathius: do you know how the Kubernetes components are run in those cases where logging performance matters? Do they directly write to a real disk or does it all go through pipes? If it is the latter, then this issue matters a lot less in practice.

@dims: you mentioned at some point that you had scalability issues with logging that went away when using go-runner as wrapper instead of using klog's internal output redirection. I bet the root cause is the same: fast vs. slow sync of the output fd. That's because go-runner always runs output through one or more pipes.

I don't know how realistic the scalability setup was, but it must have written log files to some real disk.
